1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,919
You downloaded Jenkins. You started it. And a page asks you for a password you never set.

2
00:00:06,469 --> 00:00:07,642
What is that password?

3
00:00:07,642 --> 00:00:08,282
Where is it?

4
00:00:08,282 --> 00:00:11,802
And what should you set up before anyone else touches this server?

5
00:00:12,352 --> 00:00:16,606
A Jenkins server that builds and deploys your code is a powerful thing.

6
00:00:16,606 --> 00:00:17,804
Whoever controls it,

7
00:00:17,804 --> 00:00:19,182
controls your delivery.

8
00:00:19,182 --> 00:00:21,099
So the first ten minutes matter.

9
00:00:21,649 --> 00:00:23,754
Today you install Jenkins safely,

10
00:00:23,754 --> 00:00:26,433
and you do the first administration steps,

11
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:27,071
on screen,

12
00:00:27,071 --> 00:00:28,027
click by click.

13
00:00:29,577 --> 00:00:31,006
Here is what to expect.

14
00:00:31,556 --> 00:00:35,247
One: how Jenkins is installed, and the safe way to run it.

15
00:00:35,797 --> 00:00:41,600
Two: the real setup wizard. Unlock, plugins, first admin, and the Jenkins URL.

16
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:44,859
Three: the security checks that most people skip.

17
00:00:45,409 --> 00:00:49,057
Four: your own user accounts, the system settings, and updates.

18
00:00:49,607 --> 00:00:52,316
This is objective two of the Jenkins domain.

19
00:00:54,366 --> 00:00:55,625
Install it safely.

20
00:00:56,175 --> 00:00:57,948
Jenkins is a Java program,

21
00:00:57,948 --> 00:00:59,107
so it needs Java.

22
00:00:59,107 --> 00:01:01,358
This course uses Java twenty one,

23
00:01:01,358 --> 00:01:05,519
which the current long term support line of Jenkins supports.

24
00:01:06,069 --> 00:01:07,864
You can run it three ways.

25
00:01:07,864 --> 00:01:08,762
As a package,

26
00:01:08,762 --> 00:01:09,383
on Linux.

27
00:01:09,383 --> 00:01:10,419
As a container.

28
00:01:10,419 --> 00:01:11,455
Or as one file,

29
00:01:11,455 --> 00:01:12,352
the war file,

30
00:01:12,352 --> 00:01:13,595
started with Java.

31
00:01:13,595 --> 00:01:16,081
All three give you the same Jenkins.

32
00:01:16,081 --> 00:01:16,840
In our lab,

33
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:18,221
we use the war file,

34
00:01:18,221 --> 00:01:20,362
because you can see everything.

35
00:01:20,912 --> 00:01:23,123
Rule one: never run Jenkins as root.

36
00:01:23,123 --> 00:01:24,720
Make a normal user for it.

37
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,378
If a build ever goes wrong,

38
00:01:26,378 --> 00:01:29,019
root would let it damage the whole machine.

39
00:01:29,569 --> 00:01:32,816
Rule two: Jenkins listens on port 8080.

40
00:01:32,816 --> 00:01:33,898
For a real team,

41
00:01:33,898 --> 00:01:36,401
put it behind a proxy with HTTPS,

42
00:01:36,401 --> 00:01:39,040
so passwords are not sent in the clear.

43
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:42,219
And do not open the port to the whole internet.

44
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:45,289
Rule three: know where Jenkins home is.

45
00:01:45,289 --> 00:01:46,129
All settings,

46
00:01:46,129 --> 00:01:47,938
jobs and secrets live there.

47
00:01:47,938 --> 00:01:48,648
Protect it,

48
00:01:48,648 --> 00:01:49,617
and back it up.

49
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:54,370
Rule four: use the long term support line, and update it regularly.

50
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,249
Now the real thing.

51
00:01:57,249 --> 00:01:58,649
A brand new Jenkins,

52
00:01:58,649 --> 00:01:59,558
never set up,

53
00:01:59,558 --> 00:02:00,608
on one machine.

54
00:02:00,608 --> 00:02:04,176
This is one continuous recording of the real setup.

55
00:02:04,726 --> 00:02:05,685
I open Chrome,

56
00:02:05,685 --> 00:02:07,055
and type localhost

57
00:02:07,055 --> 00:02:08,425
colon 8080.

58
00:02:08,425 --> 00:02:10,753
Jenkins does not show a dashboard.

59
00:02:10,753 --> 00:02:12,397
It shows Unlock Jenkins.

60
00:02:12,397 --> 00:02:14,109
This is a safety feature.

61
00:02:14,109 --> 00:02:17,191
Until you prove that you control the machine,

62
00:02:17,191 --> 00:02:19,041
nobody can set anything up.

63
00:02:19,591 --> 00:02:23,600
The page names a file on the server: initial admin password.

64
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:27,341
Jenkins wrote a one time password there when it started.

65
00:02:27,341 --> 00:02:29,746
Only someone who can read that file,

66
00:02:29,746 --> 00:02:30,481
or the log,

67
00:02:30,481 --> 00:02:31,350
is the owner.

68
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:32,686
I copy the password,

69
00:02:32,686 --> 00:02:34,023
paste it in the box,

70
00:02:34,023 --> 00:02:35,292
and click Continue.

71
00:02:35,842 --> 00:02:37,140
Customize Jenkins.

72
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:38,006
Two choices.

73
00:02:38,006 --> 00:02:42,045
Install suggested plugins gives you the common set: Git,

74
00:02:42,045 --> 00:02:42,767
pipelines,

75
00:02:42,767 --> 00:02:43,632
credentials,

76
00:02:43,632 --> 00:02:44,426
timestamps,

77
00:02:44,426 --> 00:02:45,075
and more.

78
00:02:45,075 --> 00:02:48,753
Select plugins to install lets you pick one by one.

79
00:02:48,753 --> 00:02:49,763
As a beginner,

80
00:02:49,763 --> 00:02:51,422
take the suggested set.

81
00:02:51,422 --> 00:02:54,019
You can add or remove plugins later.

82
00:02:54,019 --> 00:02:56,471
I click Install suggested plugins.

83
00:02:57,021 --> 00:03:00,384
Jenkins now downloads and installs the plugins.

84
00:03:00,384 --> 00:03:03,747
Each tile turns green when its plugin is ready.

85
00:03:03,747 --> 00:03:04,963
If one turns red,

86
00:03:04,963 --> 00:03:05,893
do not panic.

87
00:03:05,893 --> 00:03:06,895
You can retry,

88
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:07,753
or continue,

89
00:03:07,753 --> 00:03:10,258
and fix it later in Manage Jenkins.

90
00:03:10,258 --> 00:03:12,189
This takes a minute or two.

91
00:03:34,739 --> 00:03:36,375
Create First Admin User.

92
00:03:36,375 --> 00:03:38,078
This is your own account.

93
00:03:38,078 --> 00:03:39,237
Type a user name,

94
00:03:39,237 --> 00:03:40,872
a strong password twice,

95
00:03:40,872 --> 00:03:41,894
your full name,

96
00:03:41,894 --> 00:03:42,780
and an email.

97
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:45,506
In this lab I use a simple lab password,

98
00:03:45,506 --> 00:03:47,891
because it is a throw away machine.

99
00:03:47,891 --> 00:03:48,777
In real life,

100
00:03:48,777 --> 00:03:51,775
use a long password from a password manager.

101
00:03:51,775 --> 00:03:53,342
Then Save and Continue.

102
00:04:01,892 --> 00:04:03,532
Instance Configuration.

103
00:04:03,532 --> 00:04:08,737
The Jenkins URL is the address that everyone uses to reach this server.

104
00:04:08,737 --> 00:04:11,946
Jenkins puts it in emails and in build links.

105
00:04:11,946 --> 00:04:13,515
Here it is localhost

106
00:04:13,515 --> 00:04:14,941
colon 8080.

107
00:04:14,941 --> 00:04:16,153
On a real server,

108
00:04:16,153 --> 00:04:17,436
set the real name,

109
00:04:17,436 --> 00:04:18,506
with HTTPS.

110
00:04:18,506 --> 00:04:20,217
I click Save and Finish.

111
00:04:20,767 --> 00:04:21,863
Jenkins is ready.

112
00:04:21,863 --> 00:04:23,667
I click Start using Jenkins.

113
00:04:23,667 --> 00:04:25,342
And here is the dashboard,

114
00:04:25,342 --> 00:04:27,082
with our own admin account.

115
00:04:27,632 --> 00:04:31,273
Now the part that many people skip: check the security.

116
00:04:31,273 --> 00:04:32,266
Manage Jenkins,

117
00:04:32,266 --> 00:04:33,193
then Security.

118
00:04:33,193 --> 00:04:36,371
Authentication says: Jenkins' own user database.

119
00:04:36,371 --> 00:04:38,358
Allow users to sign up is off,

120
00:04:38,358 --> 00:04:40,741
so strangers cannot create accounts.

121
00:04:40,741 --> 00:04:44,184
Authorization says: Logged in users can do anything.

122
00:04:44,184 --> 00:04:45,706
That is fine for a lab.

123
00:04:45,706 --> 00:04:47,891
And anonymous read access is off.

124
00:04:47,891 --> 00:04:50,672
Someone who is not signed in sees nothing.

125
00:04:50,672 --> 00:04:51,864
Check these three,

126
00:04:51,864 --> 00:04:52,592
every time.

127
00:04:53,142 --> 00:04:53,489
Next,

128
00:04:53,489 --> 00:04:53,905
Users.

129
00:04:53,905 --> 00:04:55,501
Back in Manage Jenkins,

130
00:04:55,501 --> 00:04:55,917
Users.

131
00:04:55,917 --> 00:04:58,068
Here is the one account I made.

132
00:04:58,068 --> 00:05:00,150
Create User adds a second one.

133
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:02,648
Give every person their own account.

134
00:05:02,648 --> 00:05:04,730
Never share the admin account.

135
00:05:04,730 --> 00:05:06,881
I create a user called dev one.

136
00:05:07,431 --> 00:05:08,189
Now System.

137
00:05:08,189 --> 00:05:10,810
Here you can change the Jenkins URL,

138
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:12,396
and the system message.

139
00:05:12,396 --> 00:05:13,154
Then Nodes,

140
00:05:13,154 --> 00:05:14,395
the built in node,

141
00:05:14,395 --> 00:05:15,361
and Configure.

142
00:05:15,361 --> 00:05:17,567
Look at the number of executors.

143
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:18,257
It is two.

144
00:05:18,257 --> 00:05:20,395
Many real teams set it to zero,

145
00:05:20,395 --> 00:05:22,394
so builds run only on agents.

146
00:05:22,394 --> 00:05:24,049
In this lab we keep two.

147
00:05:24,599 --> 00:05:25,142
Finally,

148
00:05:25,142 --> 00:05:26,498
plugins and updates.

149
00:05:26,498 --> 00:05:27,787
On the Updates tab,

150
00:05:27,787 --> 00:05:32,399
Jenkins tells you when a plugin has a new version or a security fix.

151
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:33,417
Read the notes,

152
00:05:33,417 --> 00:05:34,570
and update often.

153
00:05:34,570 --> 00:05:39,725
A Jenkins that is never updated becomes the weakest machine in your company.

154
00:05:40,275 --> 00:05:42,111
That is a safe first setup.

155
00:05:42,111 --> 00:05:42,587
Unlock,

156
00:05:42,587 --> 00:05:43,811
suggested plugins,

157
00:05:43,811 --> 00:05:44,831
your own admin,

158
00:05:44,831 --> 00:05:45,919
the right URL,

159
00:05:45,919 --> 00:05:47,075
security checked,

160
00:05:47,075 --> 00:05:48,639
one account per person,

161
00:05:48,639 --> 00:05:50,067
and updates in sight.

162
00:05:51,617 --> 00:05:53,132
Your first-day checklist.

163
00:05:53,682 --> 00:05:57,266
One: Jenkins runs as a normal user, never as root.

164
00:05:57,816 --> 00:06:01,890
Two: you unlocked it with the one time password, and made your own admin.

165
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:05,214
Three: sign up is off, and anonymous read is off.

166
00:06:05,764 --> 00:06:09,710
Four: every person has their own account. Nobody shares admin.

167
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:15,850
Five: the Jenkins URL is right, and HTTPS is on, for a real server.

168
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:21,328
Six: plugins are few, and updates are checked. And Jenkins home is backed up.

169
00:06:22,878 --> 00:06:25,673
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

170
00:06:26,223 --> 00:06:27,687
One: the repository,

171
00:06:27,687 --> 00:06:32,007
git hub dot com slash it dash waves slash dev ops dash A I,

172
00:06:32,007 --> 00:06:34,351
in the folder academy slash lab.

173
00:06:34,901 --> 00:06:41,066
Two: the files, lab155.sh, and shortcuts155.sh.

174
00:06:41,616 --> 00:06:47,077
Three: install it, with sudo install, into slash user slash local slash S bin.

175
00:06:47,627 --> 00:06:49,462
Four: load the short names,

176
00:06:49,462 --> 00:06:52,520
with source shortcuts155.sh.

177
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:53,336
Then lab up,

178
00:06:53,336 --> 00:06:54,219
and lab down.

179
00:06:54,769 --> 00:06:56,764
Five: you need Java twenty one,

180
00:06:56,764 --> 00:06:58,502
and an internet connection.

181
00:06:58,502 --> 00:07:00,690
The lab downloads Jenkins for you,

182
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:02,620
and shows you the unlock page.

183
00:07:03,170 --> 00:07:07,010
Six: only on your own machine. Lab down removes everything.

184
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,203
The link is in the description.

185
00:07:11,253 --> 00:07:13,024
Your turn, on your own machine.

186
00:07:13,574 --> 00:07:16,944
One: lab up. Open localhost:8080.

187
00:07:17,494 --> 00:07:21,270
Two: find the initial admin password, and unlock Jenkins.

188
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:25,810
Three: install the suggested plugins, and create your own admin.

189
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:30,178
Four: open Security, and check sign up and anonymous read.

190
00:07:30,728 --> 00:07:33,566
Five: create a second user. Then lab down.

191
00:07:34,116 --> 00:07:35,950
Pause the video, and begin now.

192
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:52,375
Quick check.

193
00:07:52,925 --> 00:07:55,506
Why does Jenkins ask for a password you never set?

194
00:07:56,056 --> 00:07:58,189
Why should Jenkins never run as root?

195
00:07:58,739 --> 00:08:01,150
Which two security settings do you check first?

196
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:04,047
Why does every person need their own account?

197
00:08:04,597 --> 00:08:06,976
Objective covered: MC17,

198
00:08:06,976 --> 00:08:07,985
objective two.

199
00:08:07,985 --> 00:08:09,860
Installing Jenkins safely,

200
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:12,383
and the first administration steps.

201
00:08:12,933 --> 00:08:15,003
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

202
